body:
This could be a very helpful feature for accessibility _if_ the keyboard access part is resolved (refer to

 [https://accessibility.huit.harvard.edu/%E2%9C%8E-practice-expandable-sections])

Dave Eveland proposed the following:

{color:#654982}... a Developer would have to the work, but the idea would be:{color}

{color:#654982} If a collapsible section is going to be used AND the designer places a checkmark next to “Collapsible” then{color}
 * {color:#654982}REQUIRE the user enter a unique section ID – which can be virtually anything – as long as it’s not repeated as a section ID elsewhere on the page. The section ID’s provide a way for the ARIA controls to open (expand) or close (collapse) the sections using the keyboard.{color}
 * {color:#654982}If no section ID is entered into the section ID field provided, clicking Save will revert the section to NOT collapsible, retaining accessibility as it is, w/o the function of having the section be collapsible.{color}
 * {color:#654982}Further, make the “Start closed” checkbox muted or greyed out, UNTIL a section ID is entered{color}
 * {color:#654982}Further still if possible – provide back-end logic/checking to insure unique section IDs are being used on the page{color}

{color:#654982}As another method of addressing assignment of Section IDs, simply assign section ID’s based on the SORT ORDER sequence – which would remove the need for users to enter a section ID, and simply make reference to the the SORT ORDER number (from Reorder Page Items):{color}

 

It should be noted here that a section is not collapsible if a section title (id) is not designated. I strongly urge that this be resolved to make this feature fully accessible and usable by all parties.

Terry Golightly

