The new logic appears to silently accept anything entered past the 3rd field. Technically speaking this is a regression, as the user is no longer informed of a potential data entry issue. A simple mistake such as “[email],,John,Smith” will result in the creation of an account with the wrong name. The first name ends up being “John,Smith”, and the last name is empty. I tested this in master to be sure. If you’re adding multiple users at the same time, noticing the issue in the resulting UIs becomes more difficult to identify.

