The “LIMIT 1” piece isn’t valid in Oracle either have to use something else

I can’t test this but could _probably_ be fixed like this (might not work on really old Oracle)

{noformat}String statement;
if ("oracle".equalsIgnoreCase(sqlService.getVendor())) {
    statement = "SELECT FILE_PATH FROM " + resourceTableName +
                " WHERE RESOURCE_SHA256 = ? ORDER BY FILE_PATH DESC FETCH FIRST 1 ROWS ONLY";
} else {
    // For databases that support LIMIT
    statement = "SELECT FILE_PATH FROM " + resourceTableName +
                " WHERE RESOURCE_SHA256 = ? ORDER BY FILE_PATH DESC LIMIT 1";
}{noformat}

It was commented on the core call that this would work but it’s better to have this in ContentServiceSqlDefault.java and the special case in ContentServiceSqlOracle.java.

