This bug seems like it was inadvertently introduced with the merging of [https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/S2U-5|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/S2U-5|smart-link] . Key here is the source file, webcomponents/tool/src/main/frontend/packages/sakai-rubrics/src/SakaiRubricStudent.js, and the function shouldUpdate, currently defined as:

{noformat}  shouldUpdate() {
    return this.siteId && this._i18nLoaded && this._rubric && (this.instructor || !this.options.hideStudentPreview || this.options["rbcs-associate"] != 2);
  }{noformat}

I’m finding that if I remove the last term that was introduced with [https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/S2U-5|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/S2U-5|smart-link] as below, the test case seems to pass.

