    return this.siteId && this._i18nLoaded && this._rubric && (this.instructor || !this.options.hideStudentPreview);
  }{noformat}

I assume that doing so breaks [https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/S2U-5|https://sakaiproject.atlassian.net/browse/S2U-5|smart-link], and since I’m not versed yet in how that feature should work, I’ve unassigned myself from this Jira for expediency.

Coincidently, I assume this webcomponent’s code might be simplified somewhat by redefining this.instructor to be a Boolean instead of String.

In tracing through the stack trace, I have initially hypothesized that this error occurred because the ‘currentSiteId’ field for the RubricGradePanel object (inherited from BasePanel) was not properly initialized. And that this caused a null siteId to propagate all the way to the call of BaseSiteService.getSite where an IdUnusedException was thrown.

However, I have since observed that the constructor of GradebookPage initializes currentSiteId, etc. for ViewRubricGradeAction:

{noformat}                ViewRubricGradeAction gradeRubric = new ViewRubricGradeAction();
                gradeRubric.setCurrentGradebookAndSite(gradebookUid, siteId);
                this.gradeTable.addEventListener("gradeRubric", gradeRubric);{noformat}

And that ViewRubricGradeAction in turn initializes RubricGradePanel in its handleEvent method:

{noformat}        RubricGradePanel rgp = new RubricGradePanel(window.getContentId(), Model.ofMap(model), window);
        rgp.setCurrentGradebookAndSite(currentGradebookUid, currentSiteId);{noformat}

Given this, I’m guessing there might be a race condition between the execution of ViewRubricGradeAction.handleEvent and gradeRubric.setCurrentGradebookAndSite where in some edge cases the former is executing before the former has completed. Regardless, the stack trace in the description is citing a problem with RubricGradePanel.onInitialization. I surmise that this problem would be fixed by asserting currentGradebookUid and currentSiteId in its constructor.

