{noformat}org.sakaiproject.util.impl.FormattedTextImpl


/**
 * SAK-23567 Gets the shortened version of the title
 *
 * Controlled by "site.title.cut.method", "site.title.cut.maxlength", and "site.title.cut.separator"
 *
 * [user] text the full site title (or desc) to shorten
 * [user] maxLength maximum length for the string before it is shortened (and after shortening) (null defaults to 25)
 * [user] separator the separator string to use (null defaults to '...')
 * [user] cutMethod the string key method for cutting (null defaults to '100:0')
 * [user] the shortened string
 */
public String makeShortenedText(String text, Integer maxLength, String separator, String cutMethod) {
    // this method defines the defaults for the 3 configuration options
    if (maxLength == null || maxLength < 1) {
        // SAK-31985: New property needed to control the site title
        maxLength = serverConfigurationService.getInt("site.title.cut.maxlength", serverConfigurationService.getInt("site.title.maxlength", 25));
    }
    if (separator == null) {
        separator = serverConfigurationService.getString("site.title.cut.separator", " ...");
    }
    if (cutMethod == null) {
        cutMethod = serverConfigurationService.getString("site.title.cut.method", "100:0");
    }
    return makeShortText(text, cutMethod, maxLength, separator);
}{noformat}

See above, Sakai does implement configuration properties to shorten overly-long site titles; So in principal, that should cover the “make the UI not look bad” aspect (allthough I am not sure, if every tool, every template in sakai actually is using that function consistently)

Now, given that our central data-system provides us (seldom) with course titles like “Wahlmodul Sozialpolitik: Aktuelle sozialpolitische Herausforderungen auf globaler und regionaler Ebene” which will get prefixed with the semester term “SS 2023” and postfixed with some sort of course-ID: “SOA-M-2-SOP-WMD-ILV” based on that 99 character limitation we currently had to truncate it to

*Current:* “SS 2026 Wahlmodul Sozialpolitik: Aktuelle sozialpolitische Herausforderungen auf globaler und regi“ 

in order to fit it into the 99 char-limit in the database of Sakai;

Since we do not want to loose that Course-ID-Suffix “SOA-M-2-SOP-WMD-ILV” we changed that truncation logic between our system and sakai to ensure that last part is kept, within those 99 chars and produce:

*New:* "SS 2023 Wahlmodul Sozialpolitik: Aktuelle sozialpolitische Herausforderungen a..SOA-M-2-SOP-WMD-ILV"

If Sakai would use 255 chars for that field instead, we might have been able to go without any truncation between systems - to be fair this alone is not a strong argument to make that field longer in sakai; yet again 99 characters seem a bit more random than 255 characters.

We have mitigated this on our side, by warning users about entering course titles in our data-leading system exceeding 65 characters (+ prefix and + postfix ~ 99 chars) and hint them that this “might lead to truncation in Sakai sites”.


All that said, feel free to close the ticket, as we’ve managed to find a good solution!

Thank you!

